   "subject": "Re: [pdf plots] Ancestral state in black",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi -- apologies that I totally missed this -- but black I think indicates the null state, which suggests you are running the so-called &quot;DEC*&quot; model which removes the null range from the state space.  An estimate of e=5 suggests this also, since typically e heads to infinity when the null range is excluded (see full discussion in Massana et al on bioRxiv). <div><br></div><div>Switching to standard DEC with include_null_range=TRUE should fix the general issue, or changing the plot_BioGeoBEARS_results input to have include_null_range=FALSE should fix the plotting issue with DEC*. (from memory)</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Nick</div>"
    ],
    [
